        <mxCell id="note1" value="Colors = layers (a layer only calls the one below it)&#10;Blue: HTTP. Routes, and app.py, which puts the parts together&#10;Purple: the shapes of requests, with their validation&#10;Green: the rules, and the login check against user-service&#10;Yellow: database access (interfaces, MongoDB and in-memory versions)&#10;Grey: start-up, settings, plain data&#10;Red: errors&#10;&#10;Python modules that hold functions rather than a class are drawn as &lt;&lt;module&gt;&gt;.&#10;Not drawn: every layer may raise the red errors; errors.py answers them in one place.&#10;Not drawn, to keep lines from crossing: routes.py also calls ReviewService;&#10;BookService reads RatingTotals from ReviewRepository; ReviewService asks&#10;BookRepository whether the book exists." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1380" width="660" height="230" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
